  "notes": [
    "sky.launch returns after 'Setup detached.' + 'Job submitted' \u2014 it does NOT wait for Task.setup, so create_instance returned status=starting and opened its ssh tunnel while the ComfyUI/Wan setup was still running detached. This settles Phase A fragility item 2.",
    "'Docker container is up.' landed inside the 228 s to UP, so the 7.4 GB compressed runpod/pytorch cuda-devel image pinned by this config's engine fits and pulls fine on the 30 GB disk sky picks. Phase A fragility item 5 does not bite at the reach-UP stage.",
    "The util probe's `top` idle parse works on the real image: the t+228 s sample extracted 100.0 from '100.0 id' (Phase A fragility item 3). It read 100% idle because setup is detached and had only just been dispatched; the >=3-consecutive-probe rule correctly did not fire, and the smoke broke out on ready in the same pass.",
    "ssh to the cluster alias is unresolvable until sky finishes provisioning (t+76 s and t+152 s samples), so utilisation before UP is structurally unobservable on this provider \u2014 the sky cluster status is the only health signal available in that window."
